# ScanSnap button polling service: started when a ScanSnap is connected,
# stopped when it is disconnected.
#
# Matches any Fujitsu ScanSnap by vendor ID (04c5) and product string, so the
# rule is not tied to a specific model.
#
# No RUN and no user name: the rule only tags the device for systemd and gives
# it the alias /dev/scansnap. The user manager of every logged-in user then
# starts scan-button.service (SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS), and the unit's
# BindsTo=dev-scansnap.device stops it again when the scanner goes away.
#
# Deliberately no ACTION=="add": a rule that sets TAG+="systemd" must also
# match "change" events, or the device unit disappears after the first one
# (e.g. from `udevadm trigger`). On "remove" the attributes are gone, so the
# rule doesn't match, and systemd stops the bound service by itself.
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="usb_device", ATTR{idVendor}=="04c5", ATTR{product}=="*ScanSnap*", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_ALIAS}+="/dev/scansnap", ENV{SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS}+="scan-button.service"
